 restrict qualifiers to pointers in distance loop to help vectorization? We can declare local pointers as float *restrict all_dists etc. In C99, use 'restrict'. Since compiler may benefit.\n\nLet's craft code:\n\n#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <stddef.h>\n\nstatic void heap_push(float *dist_heap, char *label_heap, int *heap_size, float d, char label) { ... }\nstatic void heap_replace_root(...)\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    long total_points = 0;\n    for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) total_points += groups[gi].length;\n\n    if (total_points == 0) return -1; // or handle\n\n    float *all_dists = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total_points);\n    char *all_labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * total_points);\n\n    long idx = 0;\n    for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\n        Group g = groups[gi];\n        float px = to_evaluate.x, py = to_evaluate.y;\n        Point *pts = g.points;\n        // vectorizable loop\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float dx = pts[j].x - px;\n            float dy = pts[j].y - py;\n            all_dists[idx + j] = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n            all_labels[idx + j] = g.label;\n        }\n        idx += g.length;\n    }\n\n    // top-k selection\n    float *dist_heap = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char *label_heap = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n\n    int heap_size = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        dist_heap[i] = -1.0f;\n        label_heap[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (long i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n        float d = all_dists[i];\n        if (heap_size < k) {\n            heap_push(dist_heap, label_heap, &heap_size, d, all_labels[i]);\n        } else if (d < dist_heap[0]) {\n            heap_replace_root(dist_heap, label_heap, k, d, all_labels[i]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(all_dists);\n    free(all_labels);\n\n    qsort(label_heap, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = label_heap[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (label_heap[i] != label_heap[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = label_heap[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = label_heap[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(dist_heap);\n    free(label_heap);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nBut note: #pragma omp simd may require OpenMP enabled; if not, it's ignored. We can also use compiler auto-vectorization without pragma.\n\nPotential issue: all_dists and all_labels arrays are indexed with idx+j inside loop; compiler might not vectorize because of potential alias? But they are separate arrays, no overlap. Should be fine.\n\nWe could also avoid storing labels array by processing groups sequentially into heap directly, but then distance computation would be interleaved with heap operations preventing vectorization. So this separation is good.\n\nMemory: total_points may be large (millions), allocating two arrays of size N floats and chars ~5N bytes; okay.\n\nNow we need to ensure correctness for all inputs. Let's test mentally with example? Not needed.\n\nWe should also consider that original code used euclidean_distance_no_sqrt which computes ((b.x - a.x) * (b.x - a.x)) + ... We replicate exactly.\n\nOne subtlety: In original, distances array initialized to -1 (float). When comparing d < distances[x], if distances[x] is -1, then any non-negative d will be > -1 so condition false, but the second part distances[x]==-1 true. So insertion happens at first -1 slot. Our heap initialization with dist_heap[i]=-1 and label=-1; when heap_size<k